{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions","id":1066814,"title":"Questions...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T06:31:25-07:00","id":1066814,"title":"Questions...","content":"Can somebody describe me the process of casting the spell? (using foci)<br /> The Hollow Earth - is the time there the same as in our realm?<br /> What would be needed spheres for making a circle around a human which would protect him from leaving it? (It's oftenly used is The Originals and The Vampire Diaries).<br /> How powerful a mage need to be (Arete rank) for being powerful enough for fighting werewolves, vampires and demons?<br /> 12th generation, Cliath and etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:08:20-07:00","id":1066843,"title":"","content":"For the first question, I'm assuming this to refer to what a character does to cast magic. The actual process of casting a spell depends a lot on the mage's focus (paradigm). To your average hermetic, it might mean saying a magic word combined with making a complex hand gesture or a gesture with a ritual implement such as a magic wand or staff to draw upon the secret names of the elements and toss a fireball. To a member of the cult of ecstasy, it might mean, putting on some earphones and listening to music to get into the proper mindset to slow down time. An Akashic might have to perform a certain martial arts maneuver or martial arts form (kata) to activate a certain magical effect. It all really depends on how the character has learned to surpass the limitations of normal reality. If you need further specifics, feel free to ask.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, time in the Hollow Earth flows parallel to ours in much the same way.<br /> <br /> In revised, a circle around a human which would protect him from leaving it was Correspondence 3 + Life 2<br /> In M20 it is Correspondence 4 + Life 2 (page 513).<br /> Page 509 seems to contradict this, saying Correspondence 2 + Life 2 , but I take that to mean, you can selectively &quot;Thicken space&quot; making it hard to leave such a circle at correspondence 2 but not actually impossible to do so. (Maybe 1 success making it difficulty 3 to leave, with +1 difficulty more per additional success; plus successes required for duration)<br /> <br /> As for power, Mage doesn't lend itself well to power measurements of that sort. I can build an Arete 3 starting mage that could easily hold its own against werewolves and vampires so long as the player is careful. How effective the mage is is far more dependent on preparation and creativity. Arete helps, but spending a few hours preparing for something is a much bigger help. A better indicator would be the highest level in the highest sphere the mage has (this is limited by Arete though), with 2 granting basic capability in the field, 3 making them fairly powerful, 4 making them ridiculously powerful, and 5 giving them the sorts of powers you wouldn't normally give players in other RPGs. That said, a mage caught unprepared will still lose to most any foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:25:43-07:00","id":1066855,"title":"","content":"I'mplaying in the community where demons, vampires, werewolves and hybrids exist. All played by players. <br /> What spheres you suggest me? Is it smart to roleplay a Orphan,?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","user":"Goran.","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:30:44-07:00","id":1066897,"title":"","content":"Hard to say. I would normally say get the spheres you can most easily wrap your head around and be part of the tradition or disparate group with the paradigm/foci most familiar to you. That way, thinking up new and inventive ways to use your powers will not be too difficult.<br /> <br /> Do any particular sorts of magical effects appeal to you? I could probably help you with cool effects around a sphere you kinda like. I personally like Life 3, because of all the cool powers it lets you add to your body, because of the stuff you can do to simple creatures, and because few things motivate other members of the group defend you like the ability to their heal wounds. I know someone whose build revolved around Time 3, Entropy 3 and guns. Correspondence is one way to stay out of harms way. Spirit is awesome if you are an able negotiator.<br /> <br /> The only advantage I see to being an Orphan is that you would usually be considered more or less neutral by some supernaturals. Unless you want to be an unofficial member of one of the other groups already in the game, it's probably better to be part of a larger more powerful group of mages so that messing with you implies actual repercussions from your organization, even if this is just one of the Disparate groups. Are you planning to be friends with any particular supernatural groups?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:50:02-07:00","id":1066908,"title":"","content":"I forgot to ask, what are your plans with regards to interactions with these demons, vampires, werewolves and hybrids and the like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:20:24-07:00","id":1066935,"title":"","content":"These kind of questions may be better for your Storyteller, as what's &quot;optimal&quot; depends on the kind of story. For instance, if the ST wants to create a realistic setting and explore the social interactions between the splats, then going Rambo with your magick might not be the best idea... <br /> <br /> On the other hand, makin a super cautios social manipulator isn't going to help you if vampires star appearing like the &quot;random encounters&quot; of a videogame.<br /> <br /> The style of game influences starategy, but in mage this it's multiplied by the fact that the rules demand a LOT of interpretation on the part of the ST. There are tables/stories where mages are the strongest kind of supernatural being, while in others they're the weakest by far. And all of that following the rules...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:29:36-07:00","id":1066943,"title":"","content":"We are fully following the books, and which race is the strongest is determined by players characters <br /> Well I would try to keep them on distance or eliminate the threat of tgeir society to mage's (maybe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:25:30-07:00","id":1066989,"title":"","content":"To Aleph<br /> I find it hard though to imagine mages as the weakest of supernatural beings by far and still be playing strictly by the rules; especially considering a few of the sorts of supernaturals that exist out there and what mages are explicitly supposed to be able to do according to the books. It probably just seems that way when mages challenge certain supernaturals directly in their own element or dive into something unprepared. I feel the trick is to find your own niche and figure out how to get the most out of it. If you have little idea of what the storyteller is like, I'd say you could get by sticking to effects explicitly noted in the book, preferring obviously coincidental ones to vulgar ones, and casting your essential magic using rituals way ahead of time.<br /> <br /> To Goran<br /> What sort of RPG community is this? Are there multiple storytellers? Is this a sort of player vs player free for all sort of thing? Will you be a mage that only occasionally interacts with the other supernaturals? Are you going to run with another group of players? and again, what sort of magic and magical group do you find simplest to wrap your head around? Then maybe we can work from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-23-2017, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:52:37-07:00","id":1067010,"title":"","content":"Each player is storyteller for himsrlf, the administrator is a final storyteller. We are roleplaying in a small town, so yeah I will have to interact with other supernaturals often.<br /> I will try to join to the local mage community with that character if I get accepted.<br /> About magic thing, I don't have some favorite form. If you want more info about the community I can PM you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:41:36-07:00","id":1067044,"title":"","content":"Well I am curious about the group but more in the context of giving advice regarding your character.<br /> <br /> For sheer ease of use, I'd suggest you get Time 3 (See the past, see the future, gain extra actions each turn), Mind 1 (combat mind control, mess with your own mind), &amp; Entropy 2 (Sense fate &amp; Fortune &amp; Control probability to make your actions easier as long as chance can be involved and to cheat at gambling). Then get guns with dragon's breath rounds and good combat stats.<br /> <br /> If you are particularly paranoid, maybe Correspondence 2, Prime 2, and Forces 3. Then use all sphere's to make a prime 2 &quot;Body of light&quot; idealized self projection), with Forces 3 so that it looks real and can exert force on things, and Correspondence 2 so it can travel where you want it to go while you remain safely meditating somewhere else. This &quot;Illusionary You&quot; effect would require a lot of successes though and is vulgar so you need a sanctum to cast it in. It would probably require 5 successes to make it happen in front of you for a scene (and more to project it elsewhere or to make it last longer) and so would probably be cast as a ritual (see rituals).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:16:10-07:00","id":1067085,"title":"","content":"There is a mage with Time 3, do you have any other advices / examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:17:24-07:00","id":1067129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are fully following the books</div> </div> </div> </div>What books? M20?, Revised?, you include things like the ST: Handbook crossover rules...all of this it's very relevant. <hr /><br /> Small town, surprisingly full of supers (wonder how/if the Masquerade holds)...wana get rid of the supernaturals/ protect against them...<br /> <br /> <i><u>Ideas:</u></i><br /> <br /> You probably want Prime. Low level Prime allows to detect supernaturals and their powers, get extra quintessence, make everything do aggravated damage (always useful vs supernaturals), direct damage, creation of charms, transforming (and countering, if you go by the ST: Handbook) supernatural energies. If you want to face supernatural forces, Prime it's, at least, useful.<br /> <br /> Mind it's useful against the kind of mind control that vampires can exert.<br /> <br /> Without Spirit, there's a whole paralel world that Werewolves can access and your character can't. This gives them a lot of resources and advantages that you won't have nor be able to counter.<br /> <br /> Matter allows to not only create silver easily, but also to alter the properties of silver in order to make it easier to weaponize.<br /> <br /> Forces it's always good to blast stuff + get's you Fire and Sunlight.<br /> <br /> Most supernaturals don't control space or time. Thus having Correspondence allows you to pull off shenanigans they can't easily counter.<br /> <br /> Every sphere (not only the mentioned) gives you stuff you can use. There's no &quot;better spheres&quot;. Chose three/four random Spheres you like, and then we can brainstorm how to face your enemies with them.<br /> <br /> With Arete, the more the merrier. Keep in mind than with less than 3 successes you can't do much, starting mages don't throw much of a punch when casting in the fly. M20 it's better than Revised in this regard.<br /> <br /> Also, don't disregard mundane skills and resources. You can only do so much magick at a time, so you may want to be able to use mundane tried and true tactics to hunt supers, rather than having magick as your only resource. Also, empowering mundane weapons/defenses with magick it's often easier than just using magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-23-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:25:31-07:00","id":1067138,"title":"","content":"Well, continuing where i left off, those were the simpler ideas. Aleph is right. There are no better spheres. It all depends on how you use them.<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 + Mind 2 can possibly be used to make your voice extremely pleasant to spirits. Coupled with singing skills and good negotiation skills, you could probably use this to coax a whole bunch of spirits into becoming fetiches to lend you their powers.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 + most effects can wreak havoc on the world, especially if its coincidental entropy 2 and mind 2 effects to nudge tings along in the way you want them to go. You can become &quot;Voyeur man&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't think of anything else that wouldn't be somewhat complicated or cause too much paradox for little gain for someone just starting at mage<br /> <br /> <br /> Life 3 for example lets you diagnose creatures, heal yourself, heal others, do really weird things with plants and insects and mollusks, and to change parts of your body to gain things like wigs and gills and armor and claws. Awesome stuff if you are familiar with many plants and animals. but most of these things will gain you paradox really quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:39:21-07:00","id":1067148,"title":"","content":"As for magickal style: If you really can't think of anything, these are the ones I found are easy to get with for most people.<br /> <br /> Akashic Magical martial arts: You can do a kung fu move, martial arts form, or meditate as appropriate to your effect. For effects, look at any super-powered martial artist in movies, TV, comics, and video games and see if your spheres can be used to replicate what they do.<br /> <br /> Hermetic hocus pocus: Wave your hand, say a few magic words, then get a spell effect like every wizard in almost every movie. I have a friend who literally looked up every harry potter spell he could do and another who looked up DnD spells his character could do.<br /> <br /> The Magician: Go around in a top hat and tails with a magic wand and maybe a large red piece of cloth. Act like a Las Vegas magician or any street magician you've seen on TV. Tell people it's all part of the show.<br /> <br /> Technomage Etherite guy: Have a device for everything or a bunch of weird devices for each sphere with vague uses like the multipurpose ray emitter, technological optimizer, or nano-assembler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:39:47-07:00","id":1067149,"title":"","content":"can't think of anything else that wouldn't be somewhat complicated or cause too much paradox for little gain for someone just starting at mage<br /> <br /> Try with this one.. I roleplayed a mage before actually,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:27:23-07:00","id":1067176,"title":"","content":"Oh cool.<br /> <br /> Try to sell these to your storyteller. They're meant for an Akashic but you could probably change them<br /> <br /> Mind \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Disabling Strike Technique: The mage makes an attack that stuns the opponent. A mage can cast this effect on the same turn they make a disabling strike using the ability they have the appropriate ability at \u25cf\u25cf or more. This effect is coincidental.<br /> <br /> The mage makes an Attack using Athletics, Brawl, Do, Martial Arts, or Melee. If the attack is successful, one success beyond the first ensures that the target can do nothing but writhe in agony. The difficulty of this effect is the target\u2019s Willpower (Minimum 4). Successes allocated to duration can be used to extend the time that the victim can do nothing but writhe in agony.<br /> <br /> Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Aura of Detachment: The mage suppresses her sense of self, projecting this sensation through her aura to become insignificant and unworthy of attention in her own mind and the minds of those around her. This effect is coincidental in places or situations where the mage can easily go unnoticed<br /> <br /> After allocating a success per target (affecting that number of nearby valid targets from nearest to farthest), a success renders the mage virtually invisible to the targets, just an unremarkable part of the scenery as far as they are concerned. Further successes are normally allocated to duration. The mage sets the difficulty of this effect when it is cast choosing a number from 4 to 10 (before modifiers). Anyone with willpower greater than the chosen number is unaffected by and not considered a target of this effect. This effect is an illusion with almost no chance of triggering disbelief.<br /> <br /> Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Defensive Misdirection Technique: When attacked, the mage uses confusing motions and perfectly executed defensive techniques to flawlessly redirect the force and direction of attacks, rendering these harmless or changing their targets. This effect is coincidental except against firearms attacks at long range. This effect is coincidental. A mage with at least Do \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, or Martial Arts \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf can cast this effect in response to an attack.<br /> <br /> After allocating successes for targets; one success can ensure that attacks by the targets directed against you, directed against someone beside you, or made by someone beside you miss for a turn; or can be used to change the target for any number of these attacks to a specified individual. Melee attacks may only be redirected to a target beside you. Ranged attacks must be redirected to someone beside you or behind you in relation to the attacker unless you are beside the attacker. Further successes may be allocated to the Duration of this effect. The difficulty of this effect is the Willpower of the target with the highest Willpower (Minimum 4). This effect makes use of illusions. There\u2019s little chance of it but disbelief would be made with a difficulty of 4+ the higher of the mage\u2019s do or martial arts. Continued use of this counts as a running effect<br /> <br /> Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Unseen Strike: After some distracting motions, the mage strikes in such a swift, properly positioned, well-timed and unexpected manner that the opponent does not see the attack coming and is confused as to what exactly is being done. This effect is coincidental. A mage with at least Do \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, or Martial Arts \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf can cast this effect and attack with the unseen strike on the same turn.<br /> <br /> After allocating successes for targets, one more success ensures that none of the targets perceive the attack, likely preventing any meaningful defense. The difficulty of this effect is the Willpower of the target with the highest Willpower (Minimum 4). This effect uses an illusion with almost no chance of triggering disbelief. <br /> Life \u25cf, Mind \u25cf<br /> Mind and Body Harmony Exercise: After learning a difficult and counter-intuitive exercise, the mage can multitask in such a manner that she gains fully independent control of each of her limbs. This effect is coincidental.<br /> <br /> Each success gives the mage one additional action on a turn at full pool so long as the action is made using one appendage that has not been significantly utilized during the current round. Note that moving more than half the normal running speed is considered significant use of both legs. <br /> Life \u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Perfected Action: The understanding that each action taken is the result of the application of will allows the mage to completely align her actions with her will and desire.<br /> <br /> A single success allows the mage to roll Willpower in the place of the normal pool when making a Physical Attribute + Ability roll. Another success spent allows the mage to use Willpower in the place of the Physical Attribute itself, though this makes the effect vulgar if the mage\u2019s Willpower exceeds 5. Further successes may go towards increasing the Duration of this effect.<br /> <br /> Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Will Crushing Strike: The mage attacks a living creature in such a manner that the pain dealt breaks the creature\u2019s mind as well as its body. This effect is normally coincidental. A mage with Do \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Martial Arts \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, or Meditation \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf can cast this effect and make a will crushing strike on the same turn.<br /> <br /> The mage makes an attack. If the attack deals any levels of damage and the effect achieves 1 or more successes, the target loses 1 willpower. A target that has no more willpower to lose tends to go catatonic for at least a scene. A mage can cast this as a vulgar effect so that it removes as much willpower as successes achieved on the ar\u00eate roll. This variant of the effect is vulgar against sleepers as sleepers reflexively disbelieves their the sheer amount of despair caused by this effect.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:35:21-07:00","id":1067183,"title":"","content":"I need something for better initiative, any ideas? <br /> I am very thankful for all of this guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:37:04-07:00","id":1067184,"title":"","content":"Perhaps that last post of mine was overly enthusiastic.<br /> <br /> If you are using Mage Revised rules get Correspondence 3 and Prime 2 Forces 2 so you can ban undesirable changes to the pattern of your being, magick you don't like, and forces you don't like from your person, making you effectively immune to a lot of magic, and most physical causes of death like temperature extremes, focused pressure (cutting), high velocity impacts, etc. Or swap out Prime 2 for Mind 2 if you are more worried about being mind controlled than being magically transformed)<br /> <br /> If not I suggest using variants of that Prime 2 + Correspondence 2 + Forces 3 effect I mentioned to make a supernatural doppelganger from the safety of your hidden sanctum. Obviously it is unkillable in most senses and many effects cast on it just won't work.<br /> <br /> I'll come back with more ideas once I'm done with some chores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-23-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:56:44-07:00","id":1067192,"title":"","content":"Mage the ascension 20th anniversary edition and how do you do that, only. <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:23:33-07:00","id":1067206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067192#post1067192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage the ascension 20th anniversary edition and how do you do that, only.<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that severely limits things.<br /> <br /> For initiative, you could use Time 2 to see the future, Time 3 to simply move faster, raise your Dexterity With Life 3, or Your Wits with Mind 1<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a thought though. What if you get Spirit 3 and maybe some mind. Then awaken the spirit of your town (if it's not already awake), of the parts of the town you have affinity with, and maybe of your own belongings. Negotiate. Establish a hierarchy where you act as agent of the town for the good of the town. Then You'll have a place in the local spirit court. Warning, rival spirits might not like this idea... then again, maybe you can negotiate with them instead and do a similar thing with the spirit of the town as the subject of the local spirit court. Then you could have a whole bunch of spirits backing you up throughout the entire game. Get Stormwarden if it will matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:30:12-07:00","id":1067208,"title":"","content":"Can you explain me more about awakening the town?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:01:24-07:00","id":1067222,"title":"","content":"(added some edits)<br /> <br /> Some cultures believe that everything has a spirit. With Spirit 3, you can rouse a slumbering spirit. M20 tells you a bit about this but only gives rousing the spirit of medicines and diseases as an example and leaves the upper limits to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> If the spirit is truly weak, or you only kinda awaken it a bit, all this will do is give what you rouse some small special properties. Generally the storyteller will give the thing some appropriate coincidental special properties. For example, you might awaken the spirit of your car and the Storyteller might determine it won't start for anyone you didn't give the keys to, or you might awaken the spirit of your coffee machine and the GM determines the Coffee it makes is better than it should be and a cup of it keeps you awake for 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, if the Storyteller determines it so, the spirit roused will be an actual active spirit with its own Willpower, Rage, and Gnosis, Essence &amp; Charms. These can sometimes be convinced to become allies or, if the storyteller allows, appropriate fetishes. So you could theoretically turn the whole town into your fetish if you play your cards right, though I doubt the Storyteller will let you do so without a good negotiation. Still, having an ally spirit that is the spirit of the town will be super useful in the town. It'd probably know almost everything there is to know about town.<br /> <br /> If the spirit of the town is powerful enough, you might get something like a mini version of City-Heart (page 635) that could serve as a Totem. (Then you can get the appropriate background and get loads of spirit help... though this might be more trouble than it is worth. See page 326 Totem Background). I think it would be worth it though. The spirits that live in the town would generally be inclined to help you out and, if they aren't already awake, you can just keep waking them up.<br /> <br /> More powerful spirits are likely harder to rouse though.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, How do you do that seems to contradict the core book a lot and add weird arbitrary requirements to spellcasting for certain effects where the original books don't seem to have such. Keep that in mind when making effects)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:21:07-07:00","id":1067410,"title":"","content":"I awake the spirit of a knife, and I get coincidental effect: it won't deal damage if I don't hold it. The door won't open if I don't try to do it.<br /> I would to need to awake the spirit of a street lamp, and his powers might be to baze in powerful light that might make vampires to flee? Am I free to ve creative with that, is there some book for spirit stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T23:14:24-07:00","id":1067424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067410#post1067410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I awake the spirit of a knife, and I get coincidental effect: it won't deal damage if I don't hold it. The door won't open if I don't try to do it.<br /> I would to need to awake the spirit of a street lamp, and his powers might be to baze in powerful light that might make vampires to flee? Am I free to ve creative with that, is there some book for spirit stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you'll get such dramatic results from awakening the spirits of things. The vital spiritual essence of an object may be awake, but that doesn't mean it's a very powerful spirit. What awakening objects CAN do, though, is make things easier or harder, depending on who is using them.<br /> <br /> The knife can't really stop someone from grabbing it and using it to cut. From a spiritual perspective, it may not even want to, as it is an object whose natural function is to cut. What it could do, though, is stay sharp longer (in the hands of someone it likes), or get dull faster (in the hands of someone it doesn't). Or else, it could make it easier for the wielder to lose their grip on it, or fly off course if thrown. If it particularly wanted to, it could even try to let itself <i>break</i> (this would probably happen if someone tried to use it on a person the knife spirit particularly liked). Unless the spirit is strong, it can't be expected to be able to move of its own will, or entirely negate the damage it does when used.<br /> <br /> The door can certainly try to jam if it didn't want a particular person to enter. It could also slowly close, or become ajar. If someone forces the matter, though, there's little a lowly door spirit can do.<br /> <br /> A street lamp will not be able to strike fear in the hearts of vampires, or give off light that harms them. That is beyond them, as street lamps normally can't do that.<br /> <br /> Awakening the spirit of an object is meant to provide the mage with subtle advantages. Generally, if it would involve it doing something Vulgar if it were Sphere magick, such an action is probably too great. Not unless the spirit were particularly strong, which would require the object to be quite old, in most cases. Happy coincidences are fair game. Like an awakened gun just happening to &quot;misfire&quot; and shoot at one of the mage's enemies. The gun can't aim itself, but firing mechanisms can be &quot;sensitive&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are two major benefits to awakening objects, besides occasional performance improvements or issues. First, because it's awakened, that object has a definite presence in the Umbra. And, thus, it can interact with Umbral environments and beings across the Gauntlet. A spiritually awakened knife can cut a ghost, a spiritually awakened door can bar a spirit's passage. It's for this reason that many users of Spirit awaken their weapons as a matter of course. In addition to just working more consistently, it allows them to attack Umbral entities without needing to use Spirit magic every time.<br /> <br /> Second, a spiritually awakened object is one that can be talked to, and is aware of its surroundings. Awaken the furniture in your house, and you have eyes and ears there at all times. Awaken a paperweight on an enemy's desk, and they can listen in on them for you. Awaken an entire city - not an easy task - and you have someone <i>watching</i> that entire city, and can tell you what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T23:32:41-07:00","id":1067427,"title":"","content":"What about the City-Heart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:13:46-07:00","id":1067444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067427#post1067427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the City-Heart?</div> </div> </div> </div>The City-Heart - the spirit of a metropolitan area - is going to be a pretty potent force within its area. I can't speak so much about them, as I'm not terribly well read in terms of Werewolf lore (where much of Umbral politics is laid out in detail).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:15:00-07:00","id":1067445,"title":"","content":"How useful city heart will be really depends on its connection to you (Totem Rating, which costs twice as much as the typical background). At the lowest levels it will appear in dreams and visions to chosen people and grant you a die to an ability related to its nature. At the highest levels it frequently provides dreams, vision, omens, and actual aid; such as manifesting personally to give advice and help, sending spirit animals and people who embody the best and worst of the place (or spirits that seem like such people), and granting you 3 dice to the ability it embodies most plus 2 dots in cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:18:46-07:00","id":1067446,"title":"","content":"M20 says that city heart manifests as Whispers, human figures who seem to epitomize the city\u2019s personality, weather fluctuations, odd shadows, rustling newspapers, eerie vigilantes or criminals, and urban omens like messages spelled out on neon signs, graffiti, or randomly arranged trash. Its brood manifest as Urban wildlife spirits (rats, roaches, alley cats, pigeons, raccoons, seagulls, etc.) and city people who embody the best and worst elements of the city in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T03:08:11-07:00","id":1067468,"title":"","content":"Alright, my support can be the spirits, but I need something more efficient. <br /> I thought about making an armor and make it able to soak aggravated damage with Prime, and make a knife that deals aggravated. <br /> Get of Fray, werewolf gift level 2 adds 10 to my initiative score(passive). Can I get a similiar effect with Spirit 3? Put it in wonder or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:25:36-07:00","id":1067536,"title":"","content":"You could probably get a wonder of that sort. This would imply that you are extremely favored by the spirits or that you underwent one hell of an ordeal to get it. Spirits don't give such things lightly. You'd have to talk this one over with your storyteller. Spirit 2 makes it possible to negotiate for such magic. Spirit 4 makes it possible to make such a thing but only by stuffing a spirit into an item. That would likely make you unpopular in the spirit world. The Shapechanger Kin merit (4pts) says &quot;you might be able to learn a few spirit Gifts&quot;. While it's not actually in M20, it is referenced in M20.<br /> <br /> As for a knife and armor, I personally wouldn't get anywhere near an unfriendly werewolf or vampire unless I had built a dedicated combat mage. I'd be more inclined to get Life 3 (You can soak aggravated damage, increase your stamina, grow wings (or other features), increase your physical traits, and heal yourself and others if you screw up) and a flamethrower or a sniper rifle, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> I can't stress enough that a sanctum where you can cast spells without paradox is important.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:47:18-07:00","id":1067545,"title":"","content":"Yes, I will try to make my own sanctum. <br /> Mage with Life 3, Spirit 3 and Prime 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:24:09-07:00","id":1067563,"title":"","content":"Hope you have fun. Just bug us if you have more questions or just want to throw ideas around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:36:29-07:00","id":1067576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067545#post1067545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I will try to make my own sanctum.<br /> Mage with Life 3, Spirit 3 and Prime 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. That's eight Sphere dots.<br /> <br /> Just to make sure you understand, this does mean that you're spending all of your Freebie Points on Spheres, and none on raising your Arete above 1. Are you okay with this? Because if this is the case, you won't be able to use any magick above rank 1, which is mostly sensory effects. Are you okay with this?<br /> <br /> I mean, I suppose you could load yourself down with Flaws to make up for the cost, but that's a severe course to plot, if you know what I mean. Either that, or your Storyteller has given you more Freebie Points for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just to explain my point better, let's look at the math. Character creation gives mages 6 Sphere dots to start with, Arete 1, and 15 Freebie Points. Each dot of Spheres costs 7 Freebie Points, and each dot in Arete costs 4 Freebie Points. As you can tell, it costs 14 points to get two more Sphere dots, and 8 points to raise Arete to Arete 3 (which is the max a mage can be at char gen). Unless you take 7 points in Flaws - which can be problematic, assuming the Storyteller even allows it - you cannot both have two extra Sphere dots AND two extra Arete dots.<br /> <br /> Further, the Effects you can cast are limited, not just by Sphere level, but by Arete level. It's possible for a person to have higher Sphere ranks than they have Arete (there are situations where Arete can decrease). In those cases, the higher level Sphere powers are locked off until Arete can be increased to match them. For this reason, if you take two extra Sphere dots (and don't take Flaws), you would have a very low amount of your total Sphere might that is actually usable starting out. At least, until you go on seekings and spend a bunch of Experience.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, you might want to go back to the drawing board and make some tough calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:38:57-07:00","id":1067580,"title":"","content":"I apply for arete through big application not freebie points, so yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:47:16-07:00","id":1067585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067580#post1067580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apply for arete through big application not freebie points, so yeah...</div> </div> </div> </div>Big application? Elaborate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:07:27-07:00","id":1067593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067585#post1067585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big application? Elaborate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This application:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:purple\"><b>Mage Application</b></span></div><br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><u>General Knowledge</u></b>:</span><br /> <br /> <b>1. <span style=\"color:white\">What is a <i>mage</i>? (100 words min)</span></b> <br /> <br /> <b>2. <span style=\"color:white\">What is the awakening? (250 words min)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>3. <span style=\"color:white\">What is an avatar? (150 words min)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>4. <span style=\"color:white\">What is an avatar's essence?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>5. <span style=\"color:white\">What is a mage's resonance?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>6. <span style=\"color:white\">What is the paradox? Why does it exist?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>7. <span style=\"color:white\">What do you believe a mage's purpose in the world is?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>8. <span style=\"color:white\">What would a mage's hobbies be? Justify your answer. (150 words min)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>9. <span style=\"color:white\">Are mages fighters or scholars? Why do you think so? (250 words justification)</span></b><br /> <br /> [hr]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><u>Character Developement</u></b>:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Name:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Age:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Starting Arete Rating:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Affinity Sphere:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Avatar Essence:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Avatar Rating:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Affiliation (Tradition, Technocratic Convention, Craft, Nephandi/Marauder):</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:white\">Character Story:</span> (Min. 1000 words)</b><br /> <br /> [hr]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><u>Out of Character</u></b>:</span><br /> <br /> <b>1. <span style=\"color:white\">Can you use any power in public?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>2. <span style=\"color:white\">When and where is it safe to use your powers? (100 words min.)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>3. <span style=\"color:white\">What would drive a mage into using his powers? Justify your answer. (200 words min)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>4. <span style=\"color:white\">Why is it important for a mage to keep his secret unrevealed? (100 words min.)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>5. <span style=\"color:white\">What would you do if someone found out about your secret? (Min 100 words)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>6. <span style=\"color:white\">What are the factions in the world of Mage: The Ascension? What role do they have in the mage society?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>7. <span style=\"color:white\">Present the reason for why the Ascension War took place. (Min 300 words)</span></b><br /> <br /> [hr]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><u>Player Information</u></b>:</span><br /> <br /> <b>1. <span style=\"color:white\">For how long have you been playing on Vampires, Werewolves and Humans roleplay?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>2. <span style=\"color:white\">Make a list of your current and past characters.</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>3. <span style=\"color:white\">Do you understand that you can be CK'd or race-changed at any time?</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>4. <span style=\"color:white\">Post a screenshot (embedded with [img][/img] code, no links) of your admin record and activity (include each personal account):</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:dejavu sans mono\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">nks) of your admin record and activity (include each personal account):</span></b></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:18:08-07:00","id":1067599,"title":"","content":"I...don't know what I'm looking at here. Beg pardon, but could you please explain what it all means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:23:34-07:00","id":1067605,"title":"","content":"You can play as high arete rating as your lore knowledge. <a href=\"http://imgur.com/A01CeWS\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/A01CeWS</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:25:39-07:00","id":1067606,"title":"","content":"Oh. That's...an interesting way to determine Arete. Can't say I've ever seen it before. To each their own, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:27:03-07:00","id":1067607,"title":"","content":"We are playing on samp server, so yeah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:40:53-07:00","id":1067651,"title":"","content":"Anyway, any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:08:57-07:00","id":1067698,"title":"","content":"Life 3, Spirit 3, Prime 2, in my opinion, makes you a great support caster. You can heal aggravated (you need to spend Quint to do this, but prime allows to collect it a bit easier), enchant weapons so they're both awakened and do aggravated (and then give them to your group), summon spirits, increase or decrease the value of the Gauntlet, cast anty-magick fields (ask your ST if these can work against supers), re-direct magical attacks with countermagick (admitedly, it's hard to do). You can sense supernaturals with Spirit 1 (Aura perception) or Prime 1, or both<br /> <br /> Remember that you can't affect vampires with Life alone. Life + Spirit work on werewolves, tough, but it's usually not a good idea because: remember that in M20, it's ludicrously easy for supernaturals to counter your magick, unless it's direct damage or an area of effect spell.<br /> <br /> While you can use these things yourself, and buff your character with resistence to aggravated and extra points in physical attributes (trough ritual casting, not in the fly), I would not recomment to go and fight with supernaturals directly. You may win against a vampire that hasn't mind control powers nor a ton of Celerity, but not against a prepared combat vampire build. Werewolves are just better than mages in direct combat, you need a very dedicated build to have a chance against one, and yours seems (to me) more a support caster than a tank. Thus don't go against them unless you know you will have the upper hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-24-2017, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:35:28-07:00","id":1067739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067698#post1067698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that you can't affect vampires with Life alone. Life + Spirit work on werewolves, tough, but it's usually not a good idea because: remember that in M20, it's ludicrously easy for supernaturals to counter your magick, unless it's direct damage or an area of effect spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I share your reservations about direct combat with supernaturals with this build, I doubt this build is meant to cast any spells directly on werewolves or vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":".  typo 03-24-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:35:26-07:00","id":1067819,"title":"","content":"Other stuff... going through the list of common magickal effects.<br /> <br /> It says you can animate a corpse or parts with Life 2 and Prime 2 or Bones and Remains with Matter 2 and Prime 2. Combined with Correspondence 2 you should be able to make a long ranged puppet body... Actually on the same principle, you could use Matter 2, Prime 2, and Correspondence 2 to make a clay golem as your puppet; Or with Forces 3, Prime 2, and Correspondence 2, that Interactive telekinetic forces illusion puppet I mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> With Life 2 and Prime 2, you could create a simple body. Maybe you can make soulless giant insect bodies for your spirit minions to possess or something.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, with Life 3 and Spirit 3, you should be able to give your body the basic properties of spirits as if these were creature features. Maybe stuff like using Willpower as an attribute rating and maybe being intangible.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 3 to awaken a disease combined with Life 3 and Matter 2 to affect vampires you could probably make something like &quot;Vampire Ebola&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:20:36-07:00","id":1067835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067819#post1067819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other stuff... going through the list of common magickal effects.<br /> <br /> It says you can animate a corpse or parts with Life 2 and Prime 2 or Bones and Remains with Matter 2 and Prime 2. Combined with Correspondence 2 you should be able to make a long ranged puppet body... Actually on the same principle, you could use Matter 2, Prime 2, and Correspondence 2 to make a clay golem as your puppet; Or with Forces 3, Prime 2, and Correspondence 2, that Interactive telekinetic forces illusion puppet I mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> With Life 2 and Prime 2, you could create a simple body. Maybe you can make soulless giant insect bodies for your spirit minions to possess or something.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, with Life 3 and Spirit 3, you should be able to give your body the basic properties of spirits as if these were creature features. Maybe stuff like using Willpower as an attribute rating and maybe being intangible.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 3 to awaken a disease combined with Life 3 and Matter 2 to affect vampires you could probably make something like &quot;Vampire Ebola&quot; or something.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could also use Life 2 + Prime 2 to create plants, or just use Life 3 to make existing ones bend to your will. Few vampires expect trees, vines, or thorns to snare them. You'd even be able to use woody vegetation to attempt a staking, though you'll need a fair few successes.<br /> <br /> I think that Matter 2 + Prime 2 is enough to direct corpses, because they're already built for movement from when they were alive. Prime is just filling them up with motive energy. To make a Golem (of rock, clay, or whatever material) walk around and act, you'd need Matter 3. That's the one that allows the mage to reshape materials, which includes making them dance to your whim. You don't even need to create one ex nihilo, since there's plenty of soil, stone, concrete, and steel lying around, waiting to be exploited to your benefit.<br /> <br /> Concerning insects, it's debatable whether they have minds sophisticated enough to be controlled by, well, Mind. Life might be all that's needed to command them. Ask your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Keep also in mind that Life 3 gives the character, not only the ability to buff themself, but also to modify their body in a variety of ways. Growing claws, gills, and additional limbs. Often more important, however, is the ability to alter appearance in a more mundane fashion. Like a Tzimisce, you can change your face, skin color, height, weight, and voice, so you can disguise yourself. Moreover, unlike vampiric powers like Obfuscate, this is a flesh-and-blood transformation, not a mind trick, so you don't need to fight against an opponent's Willpower to fool them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:23:35-07:00","id":1067904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067835#post1067835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Matter 2 + Prime 2 is enough to direct corpses, because they're already built for movement from when they were alive. Prime is just filling them up with motive energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just going by what the book said (Page 508). It seemed to distinguish corpses and skeletons. Well, you could probably animate a skeleton while it's in a corpse, so the problem is more academic than real.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067835#post1067835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make a Golem (of rock, clay, or whatever material) walk around and act, you'd need Matter 3. That's the one that allows the mage to reshape materials, which includes making them dance to your whim. You don't even need to create one ex nihilo, since there's plenty of soil, stone, concrete, and steel lying around, waiting to be exploited to your benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad on the Golem. Yes, you need Matter 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067835#post1067835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning insects, it's debatable whether they have minds sophisticated enough to be controlled by, well, Mind. Life might be all that's needed to command them. Ask your Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my idea was to just make big insect bodies or maybe arachnids. Then have spirits possess these so they can act as spirit-controlled black-widow assassins or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067835#post1067835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Often more important, however, is the ability to alter appearance in a more mundane fashion. Like a Tzimisce, you can change your face, skin color, height, weight, and voice, so you can disguise yourself. Moreover, unlike vampiric powers like Obfuscate, this is a flesh-and-blood transformation, not a mind trick, so you don't need to fight against an opponent's Willpower to fool them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! This I forgot about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:47:44-07:00","id":1067911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1066814-questions?p=1067904#post1067904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, my idea was to just make big insect bodies or maybe arachnids. Then have spirits possess these so they can act as spirit-controlled black-widow assassins or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that can be good, as far as it goes. But that sort of thing is Vulgar, and prone to attract attention besides (especially from Progenitors, who will take issue with such tomfooleries). I referred to the ability to control mundane insects that happen to be in the environment (or that you create with Prime). Alter some wasps or common spiders with Life 3 so they carry potent venom, and you can covertly take down most mortal foes. And despite the presence of Night Folk, one must never forget the threat of common folk. If nothing else, it is useful in driving away or distracting individuals, like guards or secretaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T02:05:05-07:00","id":1067948,"title":"","content":"My old mage character carried around a probiotic dairy product drink in a spray container and emporarily gave it box jellyfish nematocysts using Life 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}